  metricGroups:
  - name: $root:Activity
    metrics:
    - GR Engine Active
    - Sync Compute in Flight
    - Async Compute in Flight
    - Sync Copy Engine Active
    - Async Copy Engine 0 Active
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: GPU Engine Activity
    description: "The GPU engines shown here can all execute in parallel.\nThe GR engine is the combined 3D and Compute engine.\n"
    metrics:
    - GR Engine Active
    - Sync Compute in Flight
    - Async Compute in Flight
    - Sync Copy Engine Active
    - Async Copy Engine 0 Active
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: Top-Level Throughput
    description: "Identify which portion of the system is closest to reaching its %-of-peak.\nLow throughput usually indicates a latency-limited workload, or starvation.  First rule out starvation by checking workload launch sizes and warp occupancy.\nHigh throughput is usually good, but there may be speedup opportunities by offloading the highest unit, or reducing its workload.\n"
    metrics:
    - SysL2 Throughput
    - SM Throughput
    - L1TEX Throughput
    - RTCORE Throughput
    - Screen Pipe Throughput
    - World Pipe Throughput
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: CTC Throughput
    description: "Total CTC throughput.\nCTC is a full-duplex interface.  The RX and TX hard-wires can transfer in parallel.\n"
    metrics:
    - CTC RX Throughput User Data
    - CTC TX Throughput User Data
    subMetrics: *bandwidth_no_peak
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: SysL2 Throughput
    description: "Observe the SysL2 cache's %-of-peak, and find its top limiters.\nThe SysL2 cache serves SysMem and PeerMem aperture accesses.\n"
    metrics:
    - SysL2 Sectors
    - SysL2-to-XBAR Active
    - XBAR-to-SysL2 Active
    - SysL2 Request Active
    - SysL2 Atomic Stage Active
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: SM Throughput
    description: "Observe the shader cores' %-of-peak for instruction issue and math performance.\nALU = INT32, except for integer multiply and dot-product.\nALU 64bit = INT64 operations.\nFMA is representative of FP16 and FP32 performance.\nFMAHeavy is representative of integer multiply and dot-product performance.\nXU = the special function unit, for reciprocals, square-roots, and transcendentals.\nTensor performs GLSL Cooperative Matrix, HLSL Wave Matrix operations, and CUDA MMA.\nUniform performs warp-level scalar operations.\n"
    metrics:
    - SM Issue Stage Throughput
    - SM ALU Pipe Throughput
    - SM ALU 64-bit Pipe Throughput
    - SM FMA Pipe Throughput
    - SM FMAHeavy Pipe Throughput
    - SM FMAHeavy Pipe Active
    - SM XU Pipe Throughput
    - SM Tensor Pipe Active
    - SM Uniform Pipe Active
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: L1TEX Throughput
    description: "Observe the combined L1Data and Texture cache's %-of-peak, and find its top limiters.\nIf achieved bandwidth is low, but throughput is high, it may imply an inefficient access pattern (lacking coalescing, shared memory bank conflicts, etc.).\n\nThe combined L1Data and Texture cache has two parallel pipelines:\nLSU : local, global, surface store/atom, shared memory, 3D attributes, shuffle/redux/match/S2R\nTEX : texture and surface reads and atomic-returns; performs bilinear/trilinear/aniso filtering\nCache Fills and the RTCORE unit contend with LSU and TEX.\n\nThe 128KB of on-chip RAM per SM is composed of 2 x 64KB SRAMs. Shared memory grows upwards (starting in SRAM 0), while tagged memory grows downwards (from the end of SRAM 1).\n"
    metrics:
    - L1TEX Data SRAM 0 Reads
    - L1TEX Data SRAM 0 Writes
    - L1TEX Data SRAM 1 Reads
    - L1TEX Data SRAM 1 Writes
    - L1TEX LSU Data-Stage Throughput
    - L1TEX LSU Writeback-Stage Throughput
    - L1TEX Texture Data-Stage Throughput
    - L1TEX Texture Filter-Stage Throughput
    - L1TEX Texture Writeback-Stage Throughput
    - L1TEX-to-XBAR Cycles Active
    - XBAR-to-L1TEX Sectors
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: RTCORE Throughput
    description: "The RTCORE's %-of-peak utilization.\n"
    metrics:
    - RTCORE Throughput
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: Screen Pipe Throughput
    description: "Observe the Screen Pipe's %-of-peak, and find its top limiters.\n* CROP = Color Raster Operation, which performs the output merger color blend.\n* ZROP = Depth Raster Operation, which performs fine depth tests.\n* STRI = Setup Triangle, which generates pixel shader attributes and stores them into TRAM.\n* PROP = Pre-ROP, which orchestrates depth-testing, pixel shading, and color blending.\n* ZCULL= coarse depth test.\n"
    metrics:
    - CROP Input Pixels
    - ROP Throughput
    - ZROP Input Pixels
    - STRI Throughput
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: World Pipe Throughput
    description: "Observe the World Pipe's %-of-peak, and find its top limiters.\n* PDA = Primitive Distributor, which performs input assembly tasks.\n* VAF = Vertex Attribute Fetch, for vertex shaders.\n"
    metrics:
    - PDA Index Fetch
    - PDA Primitives In
    - VAF Throughput
    - VAF Alpha-Phase Attribute Fetch
    - VAF Beta-Phase Attribute Fetch
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: Active Threads Per Warp
    description: "The average active and predicated-on threads per instruction executed.\n"
    metrics:
    - Predicated-On Active Threads Per Warp
    subMetrics: *inst_ratio
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: SM Warp Occupancy
    description: "The number of occupied warp slots, on average.\nDo not worry about warp occupancy unless SM Instruction Throughput is low.  Increasing warp occupancy is one way to improve the issue rate, but there are other ways as well (increasing intra-warp arithmetic intensity, reducing long latency operations).\nFewer than 4 warps on an SM is a starvation condition; launch bigger workloads.\nHigher is not always better.  16 warps/SM is enough to fully hide math pipe latency.\nUnused slots on Active SMs usually imply that an occupancy limiter was reached.\n"
    metrics:
    - Vertex/Tess/Geometry Warps
    - Pixel Warps
    - Sync CS SM Warps
    - Async CS SM Warps
    - Unallocated Warps in Active SMs
    subMetrics: *warps
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: SM Register Occupancy
    description: "Each SM subpartition has a register file with 16K x 4Byte registers.\nEach warp allocates registers in chunks of 8 registers/thread x 32 threads/warp = 256 registers.\n"
    metrics:
    - CS Register Allocation (Sync)
    - CS Register Allocation (Async)
    - VTG Register Allocation
    - Pixel Register Allocation
    subMetrics: *registers
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: SM Compute Thread Group Occupancy
    description: "At most, 24 compute work groups can be resident on a single SM at any given time.\nA compute work group is otherwise known as a thread group, thread block, or CTA.\n"
    metrics:
    - Active Thread Groups in SM (sync)
    - Active Thread Groups in SM (async)
    subMetrics: *ctas_sm
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: L1TEX Data Occupancy
    description: "This row shows the partitioning of the 128KB on-chip memory per SM into Compute shared memory, VTG shader attributes (ISBE), Pixel shader attributes (TRAM), and tagged cache memory.\n* When compute or VTG shaders are running, a partition is dynamically created for shared memory + ISBEs. When this partition is full, compute and VTG warp launches will stall.\n* When pixel shaders are running, a 16KB partition is created.  When this partition is full, pixel warp launches will stall.  Each component of a pixel shader attribute consumes 12B per triangle; `in vec4 myAttrib;` would consume 48B per triangle.\n* The remainder - tagged cache - serves local, global, texture, and surface memory accesses.\n"
    metrics:
    - Shared Mem CLQ0 Allocated
    - Shared Mem CLQ1 Allocated
    - ISBE Allocated
    - Shared Mem Unallocated
    - TRAM Allocated
    - TRAM Unallocated
    - Tagged Mem
    subMetrics: *avg_bytes
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: Warps Launched
    description: "Indicates when shader warps were launched onto SMs.\n"
    metrics:
    - VTG Warps Launched
    - Pixel Warps Launched
    - Sync Compute Warps Launched
    - Async Compute Warps Launched
    subMetrics: *warps_count
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: Threads Launched
    description: "Indicates when shader threads were launched onto SMs, and the degree of unused (masked off) thread at warp launch time.\n"
    metrics:
    - Threads Launched, CS+VTG
    - Threads Launched, Pixels with Coverage
    - Threads Launched, Pixel Helper Threads
    - Threads Launched Masked Off
    subMetrics: *threads_count
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: Threads Launched Per Warp
    description: "Indicates the number of threads initially active per launched warp.  Higher is better.\nIf you see low values, inspect the shaders running in this region:\n* Do any compute shaders have thread group dimensions that aren't evenly divisible by 32?\n* For pixel shaders, are there too many small triangles?  See also: Avg. Pixels per Rasterized Primitive.\n"
    metrics:
    - Threads Launched Per Warp
    - Threads Launched Per Pixel Warp
    subMetrics: *inst_ratio
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: SM Memory Bandwidth
    description: "The overall bandwidth from the SM to each memory path.\nThis memory traffic is generated (directly or indirectly) by shaders or CUDA kernels.\nThe metrics in this row are overlaid to show the absolute magnitude; however, this disregards pipeline or bus sharing.  See additional L1TEX Throughput and Bandwidth rows to understand those types of limiters.\n"
    metrics:
    - L1TEX Shared Memory Bandwidth
    - L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth
    subMetrics: *bandwidth
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: L1TEX LSU Throughput
    description: "Observe the Load/Store Unit's %-of-peak, and find its top limiters.\nIf LSU Data > LSU Writeback, it's likely poor address coalescing (local / global / surface), or high bank conflicts (shared).\nIf LSU Writeback > LSU Data, it's likely due to 64-bit or 128-bit uniform loads.\n"
    metrics:
    - L1TEX LSU Data-Stage Throughput
    - L1TEX LSU Writeback-Stage Throughput
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: L1TEX LSU Throughput per Memory Space
    description: "Determine the main contributor to high LSU throughput.\nLocal memory is used by indexed per-thread arrays, and compiler spills when out-of-registers.\nGlobal memory corresponds to certain types of buffers, like byte addressed buffers.\nShared memory is groupshared in HLSL, or 'shared\" in GLSL.\nAttributes are for any 3D shaders - VTG or Pixel.\nWave Intrinsics include shuffles and warp-level reductions.\nSurface stores include things like RWTexture2D writes.  Includes surface atomics as well.\n"
    metrics:
    - L1TEX Local+Global Data-Stage Throughput
    - L1TEX LSU Data Wavefronts for Shared+Attribute Memory
    - L1TEX LSU Data Wavefronts for Wave Intrinsics + Misc
    - L1TEX Surface Data-Stage Throughput
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: Local/Global/Texture/Surface Bandwidth
    description: "Bandwidth requests to \"tagged\" memory spaces that reside in main memory.\nIncludes local, global, texture, and surface memory accesses.\nDoes not include shared memory or 3D attributes.\n"
    metrics:
    - L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth
    - L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth (miss)
    - SysL2 Total from L1TEX
    - SysL2 Misses from L1TEX
    subMetrics: *bandwidth
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth per Hit/Miss
    description: "Bandwidth requests to \"tagged\" data memory spaces that reside in main memory, decomposed into hit and miss bandwidth.\nTagged data memory includes local, global, texture, and surface memory accesses.\n"
    metrics:
    - L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth (hit)
    - L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth (miss)
    subMetrics: *bandwidth
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: L2 Sector Hit-Rates from L1TEX
    description: "If the hit-rates in this row are low, it means data accesses are missing in both the L1TEX cache and the L2 cache.  These accesses will pay the full latency penalty of a main memory access (to system memory or video memory).\n"
    metrics:
    - SysL2 Sector Hit-Rate from L1TEX Reads
    - SysL2 Sector Hit-Rate from L1TEX Writes
    - SysL2 Sector Hit-Rate from L1TEX Atomics
    subMetrics: *ratio
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: L1TEX Cache Capacity per Warp
    description: "The average L1Data cache available per resident warp.\nIf the L1TEX Tag-Stage Sector Hit-Rate is low, this per-warp capacity is being exceeded.\n"
    metrics:
    - L1Data Space per Warp
    subMetrics: *capacity
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: GCC Bandwidth
    description: "The GCC is a mid-level cache for constant, instruction, and texture/surface descriptor memory.  It sits between the corresponding L1 caches (DCC, IDC, ICC, TSL1) and the L2 caches.\nThis row shows the overall bandwidth for these memory spaces, and the flow through the cache hierarchy.\n"
    metrics:
    - SysL2 Bandwidth from GCC
    - SysL2 Sector Misses from GCC
    subMetrics: *bandwidth
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: GCC Bandwidth per Type
    description: "The GCC Constant Cache's bandwidth is proportional to miss-traffic from various L1 caches in the SMs.\n[128-bytes / cycle] Instruction requests come from the SM L1I$, aka ICC.\n[  64-bytes / cycle] Constant requests come from the DCC (scalar constant cache) or IDC (indexed constant cache).\n"
    metrics:
    - GCC Inst Bandwidth
    - GCC Constant Bandwidth
    subMetrics: *bandwidth
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: GCC Hit-Rates
    description: "Observe the hit-rate of each memory space served by the GCC cache:\nIf low instruction hit-rate: consider reducing loop unrolling, force-no-inline, or trying shader subroutines / callable shaders [in ray tracing].\nIf low constant hit-rate: consider compacting data into 64B or 256B aligned regions (cache & prefetch-friendly), and reducing indexed constant loads.\n"
    metrics:
    - GCC Constant Hit-Rate
    subMetrics: *ratio
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: GCC Tag-Stage Miss-Bandwidth per Type
    description: "The approximate miss bandwidth from GCC to L2.\nThis row shows tag misses, not true misses.\n"
    metrics:
    - GCC Inst Miss Bandwidth
    - GCC Constant Miss Bandwidth
    subMetrics: *bandwidth
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: Compute Engine
    description: "This row indicates whether a compute dispatch is in the pipeline, per queue family.\nA dispatch that was started, but hasn't yet launched a thread group, will be counted here.\nDispatches may be queued for a long time, before launching their first thread group.\n"
    metrics:
    - Sync Compute in Flight
    - Async Compute in Flight
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: CWD Thread Groups Launched
    description: "This row indicates when CTAs were launched from CWD to the SMs.\n"
    metrics:
    - Sync CTAs launched
    - Async CTAs launched
    subMetrics: *ctas
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: 3D Engine
    description: "This row indicates when the 3D engine was active.\n"
    metrics:
    - Screen Pipe Throughput
    - World Pipe Throughput
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: CROP Blended Pixels
    description: "This row shows the number of color pixels sent to CROP for color blending.\nWhen multiple render targets (MRT) are in use, the ratio of CROP Pixels / Z-Passed Pixels ~= #MRT. In other words, the number of pixels reported increses for each zpassed-pixel, for each render target.\n"
    metrics:
    - CROP Input Pixels
    subMetrics: *pixels
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: Depth Pixel Data Flow
    description: "Observe the creation and reduction of work through Raster, Shading, and ROP.\nThe rasterizer has a max rate of 64 pixels/cycle/GPC, divided by the MSAA level.\nThe color ROP pipeline has a max rate of 16 pixels/cycle/GPC.\n"
    metrics:
    - ZROP Input Pixels
    subMetrics: *pixels
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: Primitive Data Flow
    description: "Observe the World Pipe's %-of-peak, and find its top limiters.\n* PD = Primitive Distributor, which performs input assembly work.\n"
    metrics:
    - PDA Primitives In
    - Vertex Shaded Primitives
    subMetrics: *primitive_rate
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: L2 Bandwidth from 3D Units
    description: "L2 Bandwidth from all 3D fixed-function units.\n"
    metrics:
    - SysL2 Bandwidth from PE
    - SysL2 Bandwidth from Raster
    - SysL2 Bandwidth from ZROP
    - SysL2 Bandwidth from CROP
    subMetrics: *bandwidth
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: L2 Sector Hit-Rates from 3D Units
    description: "Low L2 Hit-Rates from fixed-function 3D units may imply the following:\n* In general, memory pages marked as \"GPU uncacheable\"\n* In general, use of pitch-linear (row-major) layouts for 2D or 3D surfaces.\n*\n"
    metrics:
    - SysL2 Sector Hit-Rate from PE
    - SysL2 Sector Hit-Rate from PE Reads
    - SysL2 Sector Hit-Rate from Raster
    - SysL2 Sector Hit-Rate from CROP
    - SysL2 Sector Hit-Rate from ZROP
    subMetrics: *ratio
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: 3D Queue Engine Activity
    description: "3D Queues have the following engines\n* 3D Engine : for draw calls. Shown here via Warp Occupancy counters.\n* 2D Engine : for texture copies, including scaled blits. (not shown)\n* Sync Copy Engine : for buffer copies\n* Sync Compute Engine : for compute dispatches\n"
    metrics:
    - Sync Copy Engine Active
    - Sync Compute in Flight
    subMetrics: *throughput
    aggregationOp: sum
  - name: Compute Q Engine Activity
    description: "Observe the active engines within the GPU, and their degree of overlap.\nThe GR engine is the combined 3D and Compute engine.\n"
    metrics:
    - Async Compute in Flight
    subMetrics: *cycles
    aggregationOp: max
  - name: Clock Frequencies
    description: "The GPU is divided into many clock domains; this row shows their frequencies over time.\n"
    metrics:
    - GPC Frequency
    - SYS Frequency
    - SysL2 Frequency
    subMetrics: *hertz
    aggregationOp: max

  timelineViews:
  - name: Default
    rows:
    - $root:Activity
    - GPU Engine Activity
    - metricGroup: Top-Level Throughput
      heightScale: 4
      children:
      - CTC Throughput
      - SysL2 Throughput
      - SM Throughput
      - L1TEX Throughput
      - RTCORE Throughput
      - Screen Pipe Throughput
      - World Pipe Throughput
    - metricGroup: SM Throughput
      children:
      - Active Threads Per Warp
    - metricGroup: SM Warp Occupancy
      heightScale: 3
      children:
      - SM Register Occupancy
      - SM Compute Thread Group Occupancy
      - L1TEX Data Occupancy
      - Warps Launched
      - Threads Launched
      - Threads Launched Per Warp
    - RTCORE Throughput
    - metricGroup: SM Memory Bandwidth
      children:
      - metricGroup: L1TEX Throughput
        children:
        - L1TEX LSU Throughput
        - L1TEX LSU Throughput per Memory Space
      - metricGroup: Local/Global/Texture/Surface Bandwidth
        children:
        - L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth per Hit/Miss
        - L2 Sector Hit-Rates from L1TEX
        - L1TEX Cache Capacity per Warp
      - metricGroup: GCC Bandwidth
        children:
        - GCC Bandwidth per Type
        - GCC Hit-Rates
        - GCC Tag-Stage Miss-Bandwidth per Type
    - metricGroup: Compute Engine
      type: stacked
      children:
      - CWD Thread Groups Launched
    - metricGroup: 3D Engine
      children:
      - CROP Blended Pixels
      - Depth Pixel Data Flow
      - Primitive Data Flow
      - Screen Pipe Throughput
      - World Pipe Throughput
      - L2 Bandwidth from 3D Units
      - L2 Sector Hit-Rates from 3D Units
    - 3D Queue Engine Activity
    - Compute Q Engine Activity
    - metricGroup: Clock Frequencies
      drawStyle: line
